From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: h713: the GPU runs at 432 MHz, not 864; model its divider

Two gaps in the GPU's clock model, both measured on hardware 2026-10-02.

PLL_GPU's bit 0 is an output divide-by-two. The H616 driver models it as
.p; this one left it out. Reset and U-Boot leave PLL_GPU at 0xb8002301 --
N = 36 with that bit set -- so clk_summary reported 864 MHz and the GPU
ran at 432. Panfrost's own counters show the real rate. With profiling on,
drm-cycles-fragment / drm-engine-fragment over a stock `mpv --vo=gpu` run
gave 913849523 cycles in 2115373538 ns, which is 432.0 MHz.

The GPU module clock at 0x670 has a 2-bit M divider in bits [1:0], as on
the H616, but it was modelled as a bare mux and gate. It is real. Writing
M = 0, 1 and 3 under the same load measured 431.4, 216.0 and 108.0 MHz.

The stock firmware uses exactly this pair. Every CCU capture of the vendor
stack, idle or decoding, shows PLL_GPU = 0xb8001800 (24 MHz x 25, both
dividers off, 600 MHz) and 0x670 = 0x80000000. Its devicetree's GPU
operating points for this bin are 150, 200, 300 and 600 MHz, which are
600 MHz / M for M = 4, 3, 2, 1.

So the GPU clock gets its M divider, without CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT. DVFS
changes only M, and the devicetree fixes the PLL. The H616 instead
relocks the PLL behind a bypass clock at 0x674. That register reads zero
here, and nothing on stock uses it.

Origin: https://github.com/cstenger/allwinner-h713-mainline/blob/43b2cdd4aa1b161a281db8b10f02ce70085e2d42/patches/kernel/0152-clk-sunxi-ng-h713-the-gpu-runs-at-432-mhz-not-864.patch (0152-clk-sunxi-ng-h713-the-gpu-runs-at-432-mhz-not-864.patch)
---
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h713.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h713.c
@@ -92,7 +92,8 @@
 	.enable		= BIT(31),
 	.lock		= BIT(28),
 	.n		= _SUNXI_CCU_MULT_MIN(8, 8, 12),
-	.m		= _SUNXI_CCU_DIV(1, 1),
+	.m		= _SUNXI_CCU_DIV(1, 1), /* input divider */
+	.p		= _SUNXI_CCU_DIV(0, 1), /* output divider */
 	.common		= {
 		.reg		= 0x030,
 		.hw.init	= CLK_HW_INIT("pll-gpu", "osc24M",
@@ -279,11 +280,18 @@
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(bus_mips_clk, "bus-mips", "ahb",
 		      0x60c, BIT(0), 0);
 
+/*
+ * The GPU scales by this divider alone. PLL_GPU is fixed by the devicetree
+ * (assigned-clock-rates), as on stock, which holds it at 600 MHz and divides
+ * down from there; the H616's bypass clock at 0x674, which would carry the
+ * GPU through a PLL relock, reads as zero here. So no CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT.
+ */
 static const char * const gpu_parents[] = { "pll-gpu" };
-static SUNXI_CCU_MUX_WITH_GATE(gpu_clk, "gpu", gpu_parents, 0x670,
-			       24, 1,		/* mux */
-			       BIT(31),		/* gate */
-			       CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_WITH_MUX_GATE(gpu_clk, "gpu", gpu_parents, 0x670,
+				 0, 2,		/* M */
+				 24, 1,		/* mux */
+				 BIT(31),	/* gate */
+				 0);
 
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(bus_gpu_clk, "bus-gpu", "ahb",
 		      0x67c, BIT(0), 0);
